course: dictionary
lesson: 13133
title: Footpath: where people walk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A footpath is a path made for people to walk on, not for cars. «Stay on the footpath, please, and hold my hand near the road.» The footpath keeps walkers away from the traffic.
explain: Footpaths can be in towns, parks or the countryside. «We followed the public footpath across the field to the river.» A footpath sign on a post shows you which way to go.
explain: In Australia, New Zealand and Ireland, the footpath is the pavement beside a road. «Wait at the kerb on the footpath before you cross.» In the USA people say sidewalk instead.
fact: A footpath is a path made for people to walk on, not cars.
fact: Footpaths can be paved and run beside a road, or go across fields and through woods.
fact: «Public footpath» means a path that anyone is allowed to walk along.
fact: In Australia, New Zealand and Ireland, footpath means the pavement beside a road.
fact: In the countryside, stay on the footpath, close gates behind you and follow the Countryside Code.
exercise: «Always walk on the footpath, not in the road.» Where should you walk? | In the middle of the road | *On the footpath | On the grass in a car park | Under the bridge
exercise: Maya says a footpath is for cars too. Who is right? | Maya, because bikes and cars share footpaths everywhere | Maya, because cars use footpaths | It depends on the weather | *Nobody, a footpath is made for people to walk on
exercise: «We followed the public footpath across the field.» What should you do on a public footpath in the countryside? | Ride a motorbike fast | Walk on the crops | Leave litter by the stile | *Close gates behind you
test: What is a footpath? | A bus stop | A road for cars | *A path made for people to walk on | A wide river
test: In Australia, what does footpath mean? | A path through a forest | *The pavement beside a road | A bike lane | A car park
exam: Before crossing at the kerb, what should you do? | *Stop, look and listen | Ride your bike onto the road | Run across quickly | Close your eyes and walk
